 "notes": [
  "Kit batch 2005+ (lane kit-batch-2005-20261121), hand-authored from the 2025-09-26 archived crops (the 2019 primary capture shows scaffold sheeting). West front (Soendastraat, crop w01-269d25, 109.8 m): panel 23 north wing -> group 0, panel 29 stair tower -> 1, panel 7 four-storey middle -> 2, panel 10 stair tower -> 3, panel 27 south wing -> 4. East front (Molukkenstraat, crop w02-89d25): panel 69 south wing -> 5, panel 4 tower -> 6, panel 93 middle -> 7, panel 22 tower -> 8, panel 31 north wing -> 9. North end (Billitonstraat, w04-359d25): panel 98 -> 10. South end (Madurastraat, w03-179d25): panel 9 -> 11.",
  "The middle's 3DBAG eaves are 12.1 m (four storeys); its set-back top (panels 16 and 96) and the courtyard walls have no crop and take otherWalls window-grid. The wing and end top storey is a set-back zinc-and-glass penthouse, drawn as a mansard face in the wall plane; the towers rise about 1 m over the wings in the photo but 3DBAG keeps them at the wing eaves.",
  "The short ends' cantilevered slat balconies are balconyBands spans at the kit's deepest (0.7 of a storey, about 2.3 m); the photo's slabs are about 2.5-3 m deep. The storey-1 corner terraces with brick parapets are brick balconies. The tower gateways are grey roller gates under a thin canopy, drawn as sectional garage doors; the Madurastraat garage gate (bay 8, about 2.8 m) is narrower than the kit garage door needs on a 2 m bay and is drawn as a storage leaf, and the kit garage door is silently skipped on a residential ground, so it is not used there."
 ],
 "closedBands": true,
 "shellRepair": true,
 "budgetTriangles": 30000,
